Optional helper — most builders wire pathhide.o themselves (append
`obj-y += pathhide.o` to the Makefile of whichever dir they drop pathhide.c in,
e.g. fs/). This hunk is the fs/proc variant: copy pathhide.c AND pathhide.h into
fs/proc/ (co-located, so pathhide.c's #include "pathhide.h" resolves), then apply.
Deliberately unconditional obj-y (no CONFIG_PATHHIDE), so nothing lands in
/proc/config.gz that could out the patch.

Dry-run at -F0 against all five pinned OnePlus trees and AOSP common
android12-5.10 through android16-6.12: applies at fuzz 0 everywhere, and
co-exists with _ghost's fs/proc/Makefile hunk in either order (they are anchored
apart, so the second one picks up an offset of 1, which -F0 accepts).

--- a/fs/proc/Makefile
+++ b/fs/proc/Makefile
@@ -6,2 +6,3 @@
 obj-y   += proc.o
+obj-y   += pathhide.o

